#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:5
#: 68d8b9eb7b10445cac77b17ad02a36e4
msgid "Startup Scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:7
#: ff05a39fde6e49ec90ef65d39f6abc33
msgid "MAVProxy is capable of executing a script (of MAVProxy commands) on startup. This can save the effort of (re)setting up the MAVProxy environment for each flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:11
#: 74cd02aa6f9843b3a9b279745543304f
msgid "A script (:file:`mavinit.scr`) should be placed in an aircraft directory (ie. :file:`./Aircraftname/mavinit.scr`) containing the commands. Any normal MAVProxy commands can be placed in here. Note that the --aircraft option must be used in the MAVProxy to begin its execution, in order for MAVProxy to find the script in the appropriate aircraft directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:17
#: 8475c08ff98d481d979f6d8fe49c29b6
msgid "This script is run at startup and doesn't wait for a vehicle to connect. This script cannot be used to automate configuration of the vehicle or simulation. It will only to configure the MAVProxy options/settings such as additional modules loaded, aliases, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:21
#: 3527d2b9ab8344788af550125b1368a8
msgid "Alternatively, the :file:`.mavinit.scr` can be placed in the user's home directory (ie. :file:`/home/username` in Linux or :file:`C:\\\\Users\\\\username\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\MAVProxy` in Windows) and will be loaded with MAVProxy regardless of the --aircraft option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:26
#: 07b777d89573475a87cde51c3fc6828f
msgid "An example script can be found `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/MAVProxy/blob/master/windows/mavinit.scr>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:28
#: 8b8cf3344bb4412587998a8f76f47fbd
msgid "In this particular script, aliases are used as shortcuts to common commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/getting_started/mavinit.rst:31
#: 1240f571bd994924af4576e52a11cc2d
msgid "For example the following alias definitions in :file:`mavinit.scr` will allow the user to graph the current battery level by typing ``gbatt`` instead of ``graph SYS_STATUS.current_battery``."
msgstr ""
